                   Matthew M and Zisserman, Andrew and Vinyals, Oriol and
                   Carreira, João",
  journal       = "arXiv [cs.LG]",
  abstract      = "The recently-proposed Perceiver model obtains good results on
                   several domains (images, audio, multimodal, point clouds)
                   while scaling linearly in compute and memory with the input
                   size. While the Perceiver supports many kinds of inputs, it
                   can only produce very simple outputs such as class scores.
                   Perceiver IO overcomes this limitation without sacrificing
                   the original's appealing properties by learning to flexibly
                   query the model's latent space to produce outputs of
                   arbitrary size and semantics. Perceiver IO still decouples
                   model depth from data size and still scales linearly with
                   data size, but now with respect to both input and output
                   sizes. The full Perceiver IO model achieves strong results on
