  publisher = "openreview.net",
  volume    = "abs/2402.03681",
  abstract  = "Reward engineering has long been a challenge in Reinforcement
               Learning (RL) research, as it often requires extensive human
               effort and iterative processes of trial-and-error to design
               effective reward functions. In this paper, we propose RL-VLM-F, a
               method that automatically generates reward functions for agents
               to learn new tasks, using only a text description of the task
               goal and the agent's visual observations, by leveraging feedbacks
